.TH SYS_VM_SWAP 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_vm_swap \- query swap device statistics
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_vm_swap(sys_swapinfo_t *" swap ", size_t *" count ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_vm_swap ()
is intended to return swap device information records in
.I swap
and record count through
.IR *count .
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.
On error, -1 is returned and
.I errno
is set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid pointers.
.TP
.B ENOSYS
Current `lib/sys` implementation is a userspace stub with no backing kernel
syscall.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_vm_stats (2),
.BR sys_vm_info (2),
.BR sys_vm_slabs (2)
